  "how_to_read": "A false negative with the cue ABSENT is a vocabulary problem; one with the cue PRESENT is a scope problem, and if the cue sits after the target a FORWARD-only rule can never reach it whatever the vocabulary. A false positive attributed to a structural separation is a boundary problem \u2014 the cue and the target are in different lines, list items or table rows, so the sentence the scope ran to is not a unit the note's author wrote. What is left is the published algorithm's own residual error on this corpus.",
